 " [:a {:href "/athletes/62014"} "André Firmenich"] ", was declared a professional. The event was desperately close in the fight for the gold medal. The British boat, “Lalage”, helmed by " [:a {:href "/athletes/61388"} "Christopher Boardman"] " (no relation to the " [:a {:href "/athletes/13641"} "cyclist of the 1990s"] "), did not win a single race, but held on the for the gold medal by placing second twice, third once, fourth once, and fifth once. They defeated the Norwegian boat, “Lully”, by only a single point."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Norwegian helmsman was " [:a {:href "/athletes/62637"} "Magnus Konow"] ", competing in his fifth Olympics after " [:a {:href "/results/9225"} "1908"] ", " [:a {:href "/results/9245"} "1912"] ", " [:a {:href "/results/9279"} "1920"] ", and " [:a {:href "/results/9359"} "1928"] ". He would also compete in " [:a {:href "/results/9525"} "1948"] ", setting a record with a 40-year span of Olympic appearances that was not bettered until the " [:a {:href "/results/310025"} "2012 Olympics"] ", when Japanese equestrian " [:a {:href "/athletes/12128"} "Hiroshi Hoketsu"] " competed, 48 years after his appearance at the " [:a {:href "/editions/16/sports/EJP"} "1964 Tokyo Olympics"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Race #1"] [:th {} "Race #2"] [:th {} "Race #3"] [:th {} "Race #4"] [:th {} "Race #5"] [:th {} "Race #6"] [:th {} "Race #7"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Lalage"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "67"] [:td {} "10 (3)"] [:td {} "11 (2)"] [:td {} "8 (5)"] [:td {} "9 (4)"] [:td {} "11 (2)"] [:td {} "7 (6)"] [:td {} "11 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] 